The header above calls tb/legacy/vecnorm_legacy.sv a "frozen HEAD copy".
THAT IS WRONG and is left in place unaltered rather than rewritten.

tb/legacy/vecnorm_legacy.sv was added at a324f5d ("docs(rung2): freeze
spec ... legacy RTL copies for diff TBs") and its own header reads
"Serial: FILL -> RSQ -> OUT (~6 cycles/elem)".  It is the PRE-RUNG-2
SERIAL implementation, not a copy of the pre-R-b HEAD (which is the II=1
pipelined rewrite).  The ~350x busy-cycle ratios printed above are the
same fact showing through.

So this run alone does NOT close "post-change == pre-change".  The claim
holds TRANSITIVELY, and both links are green:

  link A  pre-change RTL (c0ef76f)  ==  legacy   4 seeds x 120 vectors
          PASS.  Run by the TASK REVIEWER, not by this task; recorded
          here so a future auditor does not have to redo it.
  link B  post-change RTL (337ea78) ==  legacy   4 seeds x 120 vectors
          PASS.  THIS log.

  => post-change == pre-change for n_log2 0..10, modes 0/1/2, cfg_eps
